    "updated_at": "2026-11-07T19:33:01Z",
    "body": "Work landed locally on issue/85-box-stock-entry (3b974ea): new `cross_entry.rs` finds each hole's entry by clipping the stock facets to a square tube of the drill's half-width around the hole's own line (outermost point; the shank read at its half-width); a round bar stays bit-identical (the mesh reading only replaces the corner circle when it sits more than ~1.9% of the radius inside it). 60 box: mouth r42.43 -> r30; 44 square bar, 30 mm hole: read 39.11 -> 30 mm deep, 35 mm flute now posts. Rapids along a hole's line are proved against the per-line entry; station hops still clear the corner radius. Tests: drilling_cross_box (5, all failed before). Holder check still on the corner radius -> #119.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
