    "body": "claimed: main session (review fixes for PR #120) · 2026-11-07T19:38Z · plan: the review found the chord-band guard (`cross_entry.rs` ~101) only protects the OUTERMOST round: an inner round surface (a stepped bar's d40 section under d60, an off-axis cylinder stock, a round boss) is read at its chords - mouth up to ~0.45 mm (32 seg) / ~2.3 mm (16-facet STL) inside real metal and the #84 reach depth short by the same - a collision this PR introduces (before, those cases read the conservative corner circle). Also the per-line entry reads only the stock mesh, so a part poking out of a box face is no longer covered. Fix both; prove the round-bar bit-identity against #118's build; fix the refusal message spacing.",
